        {
          "type": "text",
          "plain_text": " (Thames & Hudson) is about the closest thing to a single-volume survey of the region's art, and it's the one to reach for when you want to understand why Nordic art looks the way it does: the long northern light, the quiet interiors, the pull between clarity and melancholy that runs through so much of it.",
          "href": null,
          "text": {
            "content": " (Thames & Hudson) is about the closest thing to a single-volume survey of the region's art, and it's the one to reach for when you want to understand why Nordic art looks the way it does: the long northern light, the quiet interiors, the pull between clarity and melancholy that runs through so much of it.",
            "link": null
